# The Haven's leaders: the chair at the stronghold and the council heads at the safehouses.
# Voice: warm, worried, practical, darkly funny sideways. The List is said sideways, never announced.
# Lines are spoken straight to the player (docs/WRITING.md, "Conversations"): who they are, where
# you are and what's going on, in their own words.

# The first time you meet one (a greet: the talk screen opens on it). One line, said only to a
# stranger (!met); the season's name (names.rzd) and a caught lie come first when they apply.
conv haven.leader.hello
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !met
greet
once
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say? bite_shown & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. That's a bite on your arm, love. Say it out loud to the house and we'll help if we can. That's the one rule we don't bend.
  say? stronghold & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. Every Haven house sends its count to this table. You're welcome if you'll help. Don't fire that near the house, and sit down. You look like you walked here.
  say? !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. This is a Haven house: ordinary people who opened a door and kept it open. You get in if you'll help. Don't fire that near the house, and everyone works.

conv haven.leader.bear
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
topic "Why is there a bear on the door?"
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say On Day 2 a teacher's class of eleven slept in a school gym, and somebody stencilled a teddy bear on the doors so nobody would shoot through them in the dark.
  say Nobody did. So now every house with children in it has the bear on its door, and it's become the Haven's mark. Most people see it and lower the rifle.
  > @eye Why is one of its eyes stitched shut? -> eye
  > @mine Could I wear one myself? -> mine
  > @other Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node eye
  say It's been touched up so often. Somebody did the eye with the wrong brush, and nobody had the heart to start again. There's a patch on its belly too, over a hole that wasn't paint.
  say It's been through more than most of us. We leave it be.
  > @back1 I like it better that way. -> hub

node mine
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: You've the amber ribbon, haven't you? That does the same job on a person. People see it and put the rifle down.
  say It goes on doors, love, not on people. People get shot at anyway. Earn the houses' trust and they'll give you an amber ribbon instead, to wear or not as you like.
  > @back2 I'll earn it, then. -> hub

conv haven.leader.list
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "What's the list of names by the door?"
prio world
voice haven

node start
  say Every house keeps one. Who's here, who's moved on, who's gone to a better house with more room. We send copies between the houses by hand.
  say It's only a list. You count people so you notice when one's missing. Bastion counts its soldiers. We count everyone.
  > @crossed Some of the names are crossed out. -> press
  > @drop That makes sense. Something else. -> hub

node press
  say Some are. People leave. People go to houses with more room and more soup. It happens every week, and crossing out is quicker than writing the list again.
  > @why Who crosses them out? -> told | half | shut   check persuade haven 2 easier:merciful harder:paranoid bg:elder,nurse
  > @let I'll let it go. -> hub

node told
  say Whoever's got the pencil that week. Some names go because the person went. Some go because the stores did, and the council had to choose who the soup was for.
  say I didn't say that, and you didn't hear it. Eat something before you go, and don't read the list on your way out.
  do learn:haven.list
  > @thanks Thank you for telling me. -> hub

node half
  say The council does. The council has its reasons, and the reasons have names too, if you know which list to look at.
  say Ask me again when I know you better. I'm not saying no. I'm saying not on an empty stomach.
  > @later Another time, then. -> hub

node shut
  say That's the council's book, not mine. Ask the council. They'll tell you the same thing, only worse.
  > @fine Then I'll ask about something else. -> hub

conv haven.leader.supper
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
topic "Who do you read out at supper?"
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say Before anyone eats, somebody reads a name. One of ours who's gone: bitten, or lost on a road, or worn out. Then the bowls go round, and we count them twice.
  say When it's somebody who stood up for the Haven, every house lights a candle in the window that night too. It's not much of a ceremony. It's what we've got.
  say? kin :: We read one of yours, once. That's why there's always a bowl for you here, and the medic won't take your Favor.
  > @stay Can I stay and hear it? -> stay
  > @count Why count the bowls twice? -> count
  > @other3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node stay
  say Anyone can stay. Sit at the end, take your hat off, and don't touch your spoon before the name. The children watch new faces to see if they know the rule.
  > @back3 I'll remember. -> hub

node count
  say Once to see how many bowls we've got. Once to see how many we are. If the numbers don't match, somebody goes without.
  say Usually me. Don't tell the children. They'd start passing me theirs, and then where would we be.
  > @back4 Your secret's safe. Something else. -> hub
